---
description: TriFlex mechanical design and validation rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Read AGENTS.md before modifying TriFlex geometry, documentation, or release files.

V29 is the stable physically tested baseline. Never overwrite or silently modify it.
V30 is experimental and must not be described as physically validated until a test is recorded.

For mechanical experiments, change one variable at a time whenever practical. Preserve dimensions and load-path features not explicitly named by the experiment.

Do not fill the center-open underside, add a flexible neck, or apply generic whole-mesh smoothing unless the experiment explicitly calls for that change.

Before publishing an STL revision, verify dimensions, mesh integrity/watertightness, and document whether the result is generated-only or physically tested.
